    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d168">

                <pb facs="0366" n="266" xml:id="pg266"/>

                <head>No. 168.<lb/><hi rendition="#italic">Mr. Denny to Mr. Payson.</hi></head>
                <opener><dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >United States Consulate-General</hi>,<lb/><hi rendition="#italic"
                                >Shanghai</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1880-05-15"><hi rendition="#italic">May</hi> 15, 1880</date>.
                        (Received June 14.)</dateline>
                    <seg rendition="#float-left">No. 32.]</seg></opener>
                <p><hi rendition="#small-caps">Sir</hi>: I have the honor to forward to yon the text
                    of the original treaty recently negotiated by Chung How, between Russia and
                    China, which has been the cause of so much excitement in China, and which has
                    also been the alleged cause of sentence of death being pronounced against the
                    unfortunate minister by the Tsung-li Yamên at Peking. Until now no one has ever
                    been able to get the text of this treaty.</p>
                <p>I am, &amp;c.,</p>
                <closer><signed>O. N. DENNY.</signed></closer>




                <xi:include href="d168-a1.xml" xpointer="d168-a1"/>
                <xi:include href="d168-a2.xml" xpointer="d168-a2"/>
